    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The only `refuted` fact in this batch, and the reason the status exists. It is the converse of F:modus-ponens-valid and the negation-free shadow of F:contraposition, and one two-line countermodel separates it from both. Note the asymmetry in cost that this fact makes visible: refuting a universally quantified propositional claim needs one assignment, while establishing one needs the whole truth table -- which is why `sat` evidence is a replayable witness and `unsat` evidence is a certificate.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
